WEBVTT

NOTE Captions are the agent's own words, taken from its trace.

1
00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:21.040
<c.say>I’ll read the interface and study the demonstration
first, then inspect the live scene and assemble the two
pairs in the workspace.</c>

2
00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:41.320
<c.say>The demonstration shows the blue hexagonal ring sliding
over the narrow white post, and the blue circular ring
sliding over the wider white cylinder.</c>

3
00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:46.340
<c.say>I’ll do the hexagonal pair first, then the circular
pair, using slow vertical placement and checking
alignment before release.</c>

4
00:00:46.340 --> 00:01:05.050
<c.think>Planning top-down orientation</c>

5
00:01:05.050 --> 00:01:14.440
<c.think>Estimating wrist-post geometry</c>

6
00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:34.440
<c.think>Moving toward blue object</c>

7
00:01:55.490 --> 00:02:14.840
<c.say>The hexagonal ring is between the fingers; the gripper
reports a 46.5 mm opening after closing. I’m lifting it
to verify the grip, then I’ll align its hole with the
narrow post.</c>

8
00:02:14.840 --> 00:02:23.500
<c.think>Estimating ring center</c>

9
00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:39.360
<c.think>Adjusting ring-hole alignment</c>

10
00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:54.730
<c.think>Shifting ring and post</c>

11
00:02:54.730 --> 00:03:07.800
<c.think>Descending toward top post</c>

12
00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:27.800
<c.say>The narrow post is visibly through the hexagonal ring.
I’ll lower the ring to the white base, release it, and
withdraw to check that it stays seated.</c>

13
00:03:58.680 --> 00:04:04.000
<c.think>Moving the overhead circle</c>

14
00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:14.010
<c.think>Processing scripts</c>

15
00:04:14.010 --> 00:04:34.010
<c.say>The hexagonal assembly remains seated after release. I’m
moving to the circular ring and measuring it from the
wrist camera before grasping.</c>

16
00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:54.100
<c.think>Positioning ring grasp</c>

17
00:05:14.870 --> 00:05:34.870
<c.say>The circular ring is gripped, with a 51.9 mm opening
after closing. I’ll lift it and carry it to the wider
cylinder in two short moves within the workspace.</c>

18
00:05:52.510 --> 00:06:12.510
<c.think>Moving to next check</c>

19
00:06:22.880 --> 00:06:40.910
<c.think>Descending toward ring</c>

20
00:06:40.910 --> 00:06:49.580
<c.say>The ring is above the wider cylinder. One transit move
stopped 3.5 mm short; fresh images showed the ring still
held and clear of the table.</c>

21
00:06:49.580 --> 00:06:58.250
<c.say>I’m now making a small alignment correction before
lowering it onto the cylinder.</c>

22
00:06:58.250 --> 00:07:18.250
<c.think>Checking ring cylinder height</c>

23
00:07:30.600 --> 00:07:45.060
<c.say>The circular ring is around its cylinder and has settled
after release. I’ll withdraw to the observation posture
and capture final images to confirm both assemblies
remain stable.</c>

24
00:07:45.060 --> 00:08:05.060
<c.think>Preparing the final response</c>

25
00:08:23.490 --> 00:08:33.333
<c.say>Both pairs are assembled and stable, confirmed
in the final overhead image.</c>
